---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import WikiTOC from "../../../components/WikiTOC.astro";
import WikiInfoBox from "../../../components/WikiInfoBox.astro";
import WikiAccordion from "../../../components/WikiAccordion.astro";
import WikiGallery from "../../../components/WikiGallery.astro";
import { getWikiEntry } from "../../../data/wikiEntries";

const wikiEntry = getWikiEntry("marx-armstrong");
---
<!-- Load Base Layout -->
<BaseLayout title="Wiki - RaccStarLogan" description="A collection of information about me, my work, and other random stuff.">
  <meta slot="head" name="wiki:type" content={wikiEntry.meta.type.toLowerCase()} />
  <meta slot="head" name="wiki:tags" content={wikiEntry.meta.tags.join(",")} />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/wiki.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href={wikiEntry.stylesheet} />
  <div class="wiki-page-grid">
        <aside class="wiki-sidebar">
      <h2>Info box</h2>
      <WikiGallery
        ariaLabel="Marx Armstrong Gallery"
        images={[
          {
            src: "https://media.raccstarlogan.com/wiki/assets/marx.png",
            alt: "Marx Armstrong",
            caption: "Old design sketch of Marx. To be updated with a proper gallery and up-to-date design later."
          }
        ]} />
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th>Aliases / Nicknames</th>
            <td>
              <ul>
                <li>@b!rdup5</li>
                <li>Mark</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Birthday</th>
            <td>April 16, 2005</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Gender</th>
            <td>Male</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Pronouns</th>
            <td>he/him</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Height</th>
            <td>5 ft 4 in / 163 cm</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Orientation</th>
            <td>Straight</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Species</th>
            <td>Canary</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Occupation</th>
            <td>Commercial Pilot</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Residence</th>
            <td>Austyn, Texaria</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Hobbies</th>
            <td>
              <ul>
                <li>Aviation / Flying</li>
                <li>Choir / Singing</li>
                <!-- He's severely out of practice. -->
                <!-- He just had choir class in middle school, and he swears he can still sing, yet never actually does. -->
                <li>Military Studies</li>
                <li>History</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Favorite Foods</th>
            <td>
              <ul>
                <li>Grapes</li>
                <li>Sunflower Seeds</li>
                <li>Fruit</li>
                <!-- Yes he's vegan -->
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Likes</th>
            <td>
              <ul>
                <li>History</li>
                <li>Military Tech</li>
                <li>Video Games</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th>Dislikes</th>
            <td>
              <ul>
                <li>Brainrot</li>
                <li>Deep Water</li>
                <li>Meat</li>
                <li>Deviation</li>
                <li>Ignorance of Authority</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <br/>
      <h2>More links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={wikiEntry.href + "/gallery"}>Gallery</a></li>
        {wikiEntry.referencePackUrl && (
          <li><a href={wikiEntry.referencePackUrl} download>{wikiEntry.referencePackLabel ?? "Download References (.zip)"}</a></li>
        )}
      </ul>
    </aside>

        <main id="wiki-content" class="article-section">
    <h1>Marx Armstrong</h1>

    <WikiInfoBox title="Quote" variant="info">
      <p>"I- I know it sounds... strict, I guess, but rules are there kinda to stop you from, y'know, exploding, or crashing, or... whatever it is people do when they don't listen, eh?"</p>
      <audio controls style="width: 100%;">
        <source src="https://media.raccstarlogan.com/wiki/assets/voices/marx.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
        Your browser does not support the audio element.
      </audio>
      <p class="wiki-gallery-caption">- Marx, voiced by <a href="https://dankm8.com">Dankm8</a></p>
    </WikiInfoBox>

    <p><strong>Marx</strong> is a canary and commercial pilot, known for his unwavring love of aviation and equally unshakable dedication to rules. Growing up, Marx's fascination with flying turned into both a passion and a career, but his personality remained defined by a strict sense of order. To friends, he can seem stiff or overly literal, but beneath that obedience lies someone deeply passionate about the skies. Whether rattling off obscure military aircraft trivia or critiquing the smallest deviation from standard procedure, Marx's life revolves around structure, safety, and the comfort of knowing everything is in its right place.</p>

    <div class="wiki-toc-wrapper"><WikiTOC /></div>

    <h2 id="section-1">Appearance</h2>
    <p>Marx has bright orange feathers and pale yellow legs that make his bird-like features stand out. His eyes are a muted reddish-brown, usually sharp and attentive, though sometimes dulled from long flights and lack of sleep. He wears a pair of old flight goggled perched on his head. It is a constant accessory, both practical and sentimental.</p>
    <p>Like many birds, his wings double as arms, giving him a somewhat unique silhouette compared to others. It's a feature he's long since adapted to, moving fluidly and naturally with them, though it occasionally makes tasks like carrying multiple items a bit awkward. But I mean hey, at least he's a good hugger!</p>
    <p>He's usually seen wearing a traditional aviator's outfit: a heavy green-brown jacket with a fur collar, sturdy boots, and a scarf that adds both warmth and a touch of personal style. Sometimes you can see him wearing more casual clothing, like plain shirts and slacks, but it's usually just at home or during grocery runs.</p>

    <h2 id="section-2">Personality</h2>
    <p>Marx is obedient to a fault, the kind of person who follows instructions to the letter unless they directly contradict rules he already knows or go against his moral compass. It makes him dependable in high-pressure situations, especially in aviation where precision and adherence to protocol are crucial, but it can also make him rigid where flexibility would serve better. He prefers structure over improvization, leaning on procedure to keep both himself and others safe.</p>
    <p>Though disciplined, he isn't cold. He's earnest and thoughtful, with a genuine passion for aviation that bleeds into casual conversation whether anyone asked for it or not. His enthusiasm for planes and flying often borders on obsessive, but it comes from a place of deep respect for the craft rather than arrogance. Around friends, he's mild mannered, if occasionally prone to rambling about topics like military history or aircraft models.</p>
    <p>Despite his generally easygoing nature, Marx does not handle deviation from rules well. He can come across as stubborn when pushed outside his comfort zone, and he's especially uncomfortable with reckless behavior. Still, his loyalty to those he cares about is strong, and once he trusts someone, he'll follow them through nearly everything, provided they're not asking him to break the rules he holds dear.</p>

    <h2 id="section-3">History</h2>
    <p>Marx grew up in <a href="/wiki/eastunder-valley">EastUnder Valley</a>, a quiet suburb in southeast <a href="/wiki/san-bandera">San Bandera</a>. From a young age, he's shown a strong fascination with aviation, often memorizing aircraft types and flight patterns the way other kids memorized cheat codes in video games. His passion for flying wasn't just a hobby; it became a defining part of his identity.</p>
    <p>During middle school, Marx was in choir classes alongside <a href="/wiki/logan-foster">Logan</a>, where his clear, controlled voice earned him quiet praise. While he eventually drifted away from singing, he never forgot the discipline choir demanded, a mindset that mirrored the structured world of aviation he would later embrace.</p>
    <p>As he grew older, he pursued his love of flying with unwavering dedication, eventually training as a commercial pilot. His career became more than just work; it was the perfect outlet for his rule-driven personality. In the cockpit, checklists and procedures weren't just suggestions, they were reassurance, the kind of order he'd always sought in life.</p>
    <p>He eventually relocated to <a href="/wiki/austyn">Austyn</a>, the capital city of <a href="/wiki/texaria">Texaria</a>, where he continues to work as a commercial pilot. Though he's drifted apart from some of his childhood friends, he remained defined by his passion for aviation and the strict discipline that guided him both in the air and on the ground.</p>

